        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access permitted. Please use the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a viewing.\r\n \r\nThis spacious two-bedroom duplex apartment is situated within The Courtyard, just off Main Street in the centre of Castletownbere.\r\n \r\nThe property is accessed at ground-floor level, with an internal stairway leading up to the duplex entrance. (which is shared with one other Duplex) The accommodation extends over two floors and measures approximately 84.8 sq. m (913 sq. ft).\r\n \r\nThe lower level features an entrance hallway, a generously proportioned open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, and a separate guest W.C.\r\n \r\nThe upper level contains two well-proportioned bedrooms, both with private en-suite bathrooms. The property also benefits from attic access.\r\n \r\nA designated secure parking  space is included within the courtyard, providing a valuable advantage for a property in such a central location.\r\n \r\nThe property benefits from electric storage heating and a convenient town-centre location, within easy walking distance of Castletownbere’s shops, cafés, restaurants, harbour and local services.\r\n \r\nCastletownbere is positioned on the Beara Peninsula along Ireland’s Wild Atlantic Way. Surrounded by mountains, coastline and Bantry Bay, the town is a popular base for visitors exploring the natural beauty, walking routes and coastal attractions of West Cork.\r\n \r\nBere Island is accessible by ferry from Castletownbere and offers walking routes, heritage attractions and coastal scenery. The Beara Way also passes through Castletownbere and connects the town with villages and attractions throughout the peninsula.\r\n \r\nOther attractions within the wider Beara Peninsula include Ballydonegan Beach, Allihies Copper Mine Museum, Dursey Island and Ireland’s only cable car, along with a selection of scenic coastal walks, beaches, galleries and visitor attractions.\r\n \r\nThe combination of a central town location, allocated parking and access to the wider Wild Atlantic Way may appeal to first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, holiday-home purchasers or investors seeking a property in West Cork.\r\n \r\nACCOMMODATION\r\n \r\nLOWER LEVEL\r\n \r\nEntrance Hallway – Part 1\r\n2.4m × 1.2m (7.87ft × 3.94ft)\r\n \r\nEntrance Hallway – Part 2\r\n4.0m × 0.9m (13.12ft × 2.95ft)\r\n \r\nGuest W.C.\r\n1.3m × 1.3m (4.27ft × 4.27ft)\r\n \r\nOpen-Plan Kitchen, Dining and Living Area\r\n6.3m × 5.8m (20.67ft × 19.03ft)\r\n \r\nUPPER LEVEL\r\n \r\nLanding/Hallway\r\n3.6m × 1.0m (11.81ft × 3.28ft)\r\n \r\nMain Bedroom\r\n5.1m × 3.6m (16.73ft × 11.81ft)\r\n \r\nEn-Suite\r\n2.4m × 1.9m (7.87ft × 6.23ft)\r\n \r\nBedroom Two\r\n3.5m × 2.4m (11.48ft × 7.87ft)\r\n \r\nEn-Suite\r\n2.7m × 1.9m (8.86ft × 6.23ft)\r\n \r\nFEATURES\r\n \r\n• Spacious two-bedroom duplex apartment\r\n• Approximately 93m2 (1001.04 ft2)\r\n• Accommodation arranged over two floors\r\n• Two bedrooms with private en-suite bathrooms\r\n• Separate guest W.C.\r\n• Large open-plan kitchen, dining and living area\r\n• Attic access\r\n• Electric storage heating\r\n• Allocated courtyard parking\r\n• Central Castletownbere location\r\n• Situated along the Wild Atlantic Way\r\n• Bere Island ferry available from Castletownbere\r\n• Access to the Beara Way and nearby coastal attractions\r\n• Guide Price: €210,000\r\n• Annual management fee believed to be approximately €500, subject to confirmation\r\n• BER D2\r\nThe property is Leasehold and a term of 999 years which was created on 2008.  Also, the property is subject to a current maintenance charge of €500.00 pa which includes building Insurance.\r\n \r\nCONTACT DETAILS\r\nMary Cotter Gifford\r\nIrish Rural Homes\r\nMobile: 085 739 9250\r\nOffice: 028 25935\r\nEmail: irishruralhomes@gmail.com\r\nPSRA Licence No.: 002675\r\n \r\nDISCLAIMER\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
